.TH PYRA-IDLE-DIM 1 "November 2026" "pyra-backlight 0.4" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pyra-idle-dim \- dim the Pyra's screen and keyboard light when the desktop session goes idle
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pyra-idle-dim
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pyra-idle-dim
watches the session manager's presence status. When the session goes idle
it lowers the screen backlight (to 20% of maximum by default), and when the session wakes it puts the
previous brightness back. If the brightness was changed while the screen
was dimmed, the newer value is kept and nothing is restored.
.PP
The keyboard light, if it is an LED named
.IR *::kbd_backlight ,
goes off when the session goes idle and comes back on when it wakes, unless
it was changed in the meantime. At start, once mate-power-manager is on the
session bus (it sets the light to 100% at login on AC), the light is set to
the level at login from the configuration file.
.PP
It sets the brightness through logind, so it runs as the logged-in user
and needs no root. It is normally started by the
.B pyra-idle-dim.service
systemd user unit, which the package enables for every user.
.PP
The idle delay is the session's, set with
.BR "gsettings set org.mate.session idle-delay " \fIminutes\fR.
The same delay starts the screensaver and mate-power-manager's idle sleep
timer.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/pyra-backlight.conf
INI file. In the
.B [keyboard]
section,
.B level
is
.B last
(the default) or a percentage from 0 to 100: the keyboard light's level at
login.
.B last
is the level it had at the last idle or logout, or 5% if none is kept yet.
In the
.B [screen]
section,
.B dim
is the percentage of the maximum brightness to dim to, 1 to 100, or
.B off
for no screen dimming; it never goes below 1, the lowest lit step.
Without it,
.B PYRA_DIM_PERCENT
is used, then 20.
A missing file or key means the default; a bad value is logged and ignored.
Reread on SIGHUP, so after editing it run
.BR "systemctl \-\-user reload pyra\-idle\-dim" .
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/pyra-backlight/kbd-level
The kept keyboard level (under
.B $XDG_STATE_HOME
if set).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PYRA_DIM_PERCENT
Percent of the maximum brightness to dim to (1 to 100, or
.BR off ),
used when the configuration file has no
.B [screen] dim
key. Kept for setups made before 0.4; the unit no longer sets it.
.TP
.B PYRA_DIM_DEVICE
The backlight device under /sys/class/backlight. Default
.BR backlight .
.PP
To change either, override the user unit:
.B systemctl \-\-user edit pyra\-idle\-dim.service
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR loginctl (1)
